WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.568
-Republicans, from Ron DeSantis

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.437
to Donald Trump
are lying about masks

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.806
and trying to rewrite history,
when it comes

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.208
to their negligent handling
of the coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:11.644
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:15.748
♪♪

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.717
The current Republican Party
is still very much

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.185
Donald Trump's Republican Party,

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:22.121
as evidenced by the fact that
aspiring Republican candidates

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:24.957
are all desperate to mimic him
and lavish praise on him.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.926
The most popular
Republican politicians

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:27.994
among Republican voters,

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:30.029
the ones who are angling
to be president,

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.363
aren't the ones
who have actually done

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:32.731
a competent job on COVID.

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:35.368
They're the ones desperately
trying to imitate Trump

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.604
and repeat his disastrous
COVID response,

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.572
like Texas Senator Ted Cruz,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.873
whose state is experiencing

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:42.641
a major surge in COVID cases,

00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:44.176 line:0%
with hospitals filling up

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:45.745 line:0%
and ICU beds scarce,

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.179 line:0%
thanks, in part, to the lack

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.314 line:0%
of mitigation efforts

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.615 line:0%
and low vaccination rates.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.084 line:0%
And, yet, even amid

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.552 line:0%
all that needless suffering,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.253 line:0%
Cruz said last week that he's

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.188 line:0%
against mandates of any kind.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:57.590 line:0%
-My view is very simple.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.359 line:0%
There should be no mandates,
zero,

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.694 line:0%
concerning COVID.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.396 line:0%
That means no mask mandates,

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.431 line:0%
regardless of your
vaccination status.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.301 line:0%
That means no vaccine mandates.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.102 line:0%
That means no vaccine passports.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:13.807 line:0%
And I've introduced legislation,
a bill to ban vaccine passports;

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.876 line:0%
this week, I'm introducing
a bill to ban vaccine mandates;

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:21.514 line:0%
and, this week, I'm introducing
a bill to end mask mandates.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.815
-[ As Cruz ]
That's right -- no mandates.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.016
No mask mandates.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.218
No vaccine mandates.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.919
And, if I want to show up
to Long John Silver's

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.621
without a shirt and shoes,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.590
then that's my right
as an American,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.892
under Section 57, Article Z,
of the Constitution.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.627
This is exactly what happened
to Ethan Allen

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.195
at Fort Ticonderoga.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.030
The British wouldn't let him sit
without putting on a shirt,

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.267
and that's why he started
making his own furniture.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.169
[ Laughter ]
You know, sometimes when you
disagree with someone,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.538
you can at least understand
their point of view,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.407
but I just can't access
the frame of mind

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:51.678
of a person who thinks wearing
a piece of cloth over your face

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.646
while you're shopping
for toilet paper at Costco

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.148
is some "Give me liberty
or give me death" moment.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:58.918
You think the founding fathers
would've been anti-mask?

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:03.122
Those guys were powdered wigs
and Capri pants indoors in July.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.224
They [bleep] loved
being uncomfortable.

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.459 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
You got Republicans
like Madison Cawthorn

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:08.761 line:0%
saying he won't "bend the knee"

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.264 line:0%
and Rand Paul saying
"They can't arrest us all."

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.398
If you guys are so desperate

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.566
to pretend you're
founding fathers,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.301
just become reenactors.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.703
I see them in the park
once in a while.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.137
They seem like
they're having a good time.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.672
Of course,
there's always one dude

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.774
who accidentally
leaves his ringer on

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.009
and disrupts the whole flow.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.643
[ English accent ]
By orders of the crown,

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:27.046
I hereby declare you a traitor
and sentence you to --

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.181
Oh.
Hold on. My Apple.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.382
It's my Apple Watch
is ringing.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.117
Hold on.
Honey?

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.085
What do you mean, they're
out of matcha smoothies?

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.555
Well, do they have flaxseed?
Well, what about spirulina?

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.256
What the hell else am I supposed
to get my B vit--

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.424
You know what?
Listen, I got to go.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.659
Everybody's yelling,
"Witchcraft" at me

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.027
and Dave just got hit
by a Frisbee golfer.

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:43.996
[ Laughter ]
And that's today's
Republican Party.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:46.532
For a year and a half, we've
been battling a deadly virus

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.234
to save as many lives
as possible

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.136
and their main priority is

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.670
standing in the way
and making it harder.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.172
Like Florida
Governor Ron DeSantis,

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.640 line:0%
whose state has been
breaking records

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.408 line:0%
for new cases
and hospitalizations

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:59.979 line:0%
and, yet, DeSantis is not only
against masks personally,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.114 line:0%
he's banned local governments
and school districts

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:04.350 line:0%
from imposing
their own mask mandates

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:08.187 line:0%
and even said he opposed
vaccine mandates in hospitals.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.355 line:0%
And he also does
that Trump thing

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.956 line:0%
where he says a line
that the crowd loves,

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:13.960 line:0%
but, when you think about it,
it just doesn't make any sense.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.498
-Politicians want to force you
to cover your face

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.732
as a way for them
to cover their own asses.

00:03:20.732 --> 00:03:21.868
That's just the truth.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.169
[ Applause ]

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.003
-What does he mean?
Has he been

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:27.907
reading bumper stickers
outside the Tampa AutoZone?

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.309
[ Laughter ]
I know it sounds
like an applause line,

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.478
because it's short and pithy
and people clap at the end,

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.879
but it doesn't actually
make any sense.

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.481
It's like when you're
at a Billy Joel concert

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.984
and everyone's singing along
with "We Didn't Start the Fire"

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.552
and then, you think about it
for a second and you're like,

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:44.389
"Wait, what,
'rock-and-roller cola wars,

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:45.725
I can't take it anymore'?

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.493
That was your breaking point,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.328
the Cola wars?

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:52.097
[ Laughter ]
There was nothing else
happening in 1989

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:54.533
that served as a better breaking
point to end the song with?

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:55.534
You know what?
Let's just leave now

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:56.535
and beat the traffic.

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:57.837
Oh, look, there is no traffic.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.972
I guess everybody left
after 'Space monkey Mafia'."

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:01.741
[ Laughter ]
With that said,

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.009
what a time to grow up!

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:06.178
I feel like my kids
experience a full verse

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.614
of "We Didn't Start the Fire"
events every week, now.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:10.550
Meanwhile, when I was 16
and my dad would yell at me

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.618
to get my act together, the only
thing I could say to him was,

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:17.090
"Maybe your generation could've
have solved the cola wars, Dad!"

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.424
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.159
By the way, can I just repeat?

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.561
For the millionth time,

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:24.230
no one likes wearing masks.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.631
How do you think I feel,

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.800
trying to get a table
at a crowded restaurant

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.235
with the famous half
of my face covered?

00:04:30.235 --> 00:04:33.039
So I try to say things that'll
help the maître d' recognize me.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.274
"Uh, from the looks of it,
sir, we're full tonight."

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.777
Ah, well, maybe you should take
a closer look?

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:40.379
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:43.182
And then they say, "We know
who you are, Mr. Meyers.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.316
[ Laughter ]
We're fully booked."

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:47.053
How do you think I feel?!

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.121
But we need to protect ourselves

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:50.790
and we need
to protect each other.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.392 line:0%
Studies have repeatedly
shown that masks

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.593 line:0%
cut down on transmission
and, the better the mask,

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:56.396 line:0%
the more protection you get.
But, of course,

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.230
the best protection is
getting vaccinated.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:02.067
We need a layered approach --
vaccines, masks, ventilation.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:05.270
I don't know why right-wingers
get so mad about this.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.607
I mean, complex problems
require complex solutions.

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:10.943
They don't want to hear that,
which is why they've spent

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.212
the entirety of the pandemic
lining up behind a guy

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.247
who once asked
his medical advisors

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:17.116
if we could just give people
a flu shot

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:20.052
to cure them of coronavirus,
a question so dumb,

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:21.820
it was immediately shot down.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.790
-You take a solid flu vaccine,
you don't think that would have

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.126
an impact, or much
of an impact, on corona?

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.668
-First of all,
what's a solid flu vaccine?

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:37.970
Does he think there are
[bleep] flu vaccines

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.238
or people out there looking

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.174
for a Kirkland Signature
vaccine?

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.474
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:45.311
It's not liquor.
There isn't a top shelf flu shot

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.246
where they spell it
like it's French.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.148
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.150
That clip is like
a Trump Rosetta Stone.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.453
It captures so much about him
in like ten seconds.

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.721
He thinks he found a shortcut
because he doesn't actually want

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.623
to solve the problem,
it's incredibly stupid,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.359
and, instead of asking
his advisors in private,

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.260
he waits until he's on-camera,

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.997
thus forcing them to tell him
to his face in public,

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.933
at which point
he immediately backs down.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.434
I'm surprised
he didn't start attributing

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.436
all his medical ideas
to a friend.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.437
[ As Trump ]
Uh, a friend of mine
wanted to know

00:06:12.437 --> 00:06:14.840
if, maybe,
you could cure the virus

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.110
by swallowing a battery?

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.377
A battery covered in Bengay?

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.511
Is that something?

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:21.146
[ Laughter ]
Is that something?

00:06:21.146 --> 00:06:24.450
No? No? Okay.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.785
I'll tell my stupid friend
it's a no.

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:29.489
[ Laughter ]
And, now, Trump is trying
to erase history,

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:32.424
first, by claiming the vaccine
rollout under his administration

00:06:32.424 --> 00:06:35.027
was a success, when, in reality,
it was a disaster.

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:37.497
-I'm very proud of the vaccine.
I've taken the vaccine.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:39.064 line:0%
I'm very, very proud of it.

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:41.434 line:0%
At the same time, some people
don't want to take it

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.369 line:0%
and, you know,
when I was president,

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.470 line:0%
you didn't have this problem

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.539 line:0%
with people not wanting
to take it.

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.808 line:0%
They don't take it
because they don't trust Biden

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:51.043 line:0%
and they don't trust
the Biden administration.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.311 line:0%
When I was president,

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.680 line:0%
you didn't have people
protesting the vaccine.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.282 line:0%
If you just think back,

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:58.651 line:0%
everybody wanted to get it
and we were giving out

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.519 line:0%
over a million shots a day.

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:02.555 line:0%
We had that thing rockin'.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.089
-You did not have it rockin',

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:05.157
Wolfman Jerk.

00:07:05.157 --> 00:07:06.225
[ Laughter ]
The vaccine rollout,

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.760
when you were president,
was a disaster.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.995 line:0%
You repeatedly missed
your own stated goals,

00:07:09.995 --> 00:07:11.964 line:0%
doses were thrown away,
and people were lined up

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.332 line:0%
for hours
on sidewalks and in cars.

00:07:14.332 --> 00:07:15.835 line:0%
And you were totally AWOL

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.603 line:0%
because you were spending
all your time trying

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:18.871 line:0%
to get the election overturned.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.039 line:0%
As people were lining up
for hours

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:23.242 line:0%
for vaccines in the middle
of a brutal winter,

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.978
when thousands of people
were dying from COVID every day,

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:29.114
just as a reminder,
this is what Trump was doing.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:31.383
-The president hasn't attended
a task force meeting

00:07:31.383 --> 00:07:34.219
in five months,
even though they've had one held

00:07:34.219 --> 00:07:36.956
just in the last week,
so if that gives you any idea.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:39.758 line:0%
We're actually told by sources
he's much more consumed

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:42.661 line:0%
by the state of this election
and contesting the results

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:45.264 line:0%
than he is with the pandemic
surging across the country.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:48.634
-One of the president's
visitors today, Mike Lindell,

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.869
the founder of MyPillow,
was seen over here

00:07:50.869 --> 00:07:52.771
at the White House
outside the West Wing.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:54.573 line:0%
A White House official
did tell me, Wolf,

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:57.409 line:0%
that it is believed that
the president and Lindell met.

00:07:57.409 --> 00:07:58.878 line:0%
-A Washington Post photographer

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:02.114 line:0%
got a close-up of the notes
that he was carrying with him

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.882 line:0%
and, Jake,
when you zoom in on them,

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:06.085 line:0%
you can see that he is talking
about the election.

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:08.587 line:0%
Things like martial law
are mentioned.

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:11.456 line:0%
-The guy from MyPillow
is carrying documents

00:08:11.456 --> 00:08:12.658 line:0%
and talking to President Trump,

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.628 line:0%
presumably about declaring
martial law.

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.696
-That was in January,
when we could've used

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.832
some national leadership
on the vaccine rollout.

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:22.567
Instead, Trump was listening
to a pillow salesman

00:08:22.567 --> 00:08:25.137
